A cross-module reference to a block with declarations of its own resolves to
that block's one class. Both blocks write their rule, and the consumer's
rule needs the marker's class on the same element.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml m.re > m.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl m.ml -o m.ml
  $ refmt --parse re --print ml n.re > n.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl n.ml -o n.ml

  $ styled-ppx.generate m.ml n.ml > styles.css
  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .css-ziky51{background:red;color:white;}
  .css-y2nqrg.css-ziky51{padding:1rem;}
